# Frontend Testing Guidelines

## Test types

- **E2E tests (Cypress, browser + backend integration)**
  - Location: `cypress/e2e/group-*/`
  - Naming: `*.cy.js`
  - Run all e2e tests: `yarn cypress run`
  - Run one e2e spec: `yarn cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/group-N/test_file.cy.js`
  - Use for end-to-end user flows with real UI and backend behavior.

- **Component tests (Cypress Component Testing)**
  - Location: `packages/**` and `apps/**`
  - Naming: `*.cy.jsx`
  - Run all component specs: `yarn cypress run --component`
  - Run one component spec: `yarn cypress run --component --spec apps/.../ComponentName.cy.jsx`
  - Use for isolated component behavior and rendering checks.

- **Unit tests (Vitest)**
  - Location: `apps/**/src` and `packages/**/src`
  - Naming: `*.test.js`
  - Run all unit tests: `yarn vitest run`
  - Run one unit test file: `yarn vitest run path/to/file.test.js`
  - Use for pure logic, utilities, and small focused behaviors.

## E2E project structure
- Test data files go in `cypress/test_files/`
- Shared helpers are in `cypress/e2e/common_functions.js`

## E2E common functions (import from `../common_functions`)
Always prefer these over raw `cy.get()` chains for common operations in e2e tests.

## Iteration workflow
- Use `it.only(...)` on new/failing Cypress tests to skip the rest of the suite during development.
- Prefer targeting a single spec while iterating:
  - E2E: `yarn cypress run --spec cypress/e2e/group-N/test_file.cy.js`
  - Component: `yarn cypress run --component --spec apps/.../ComponentName.cy.jsx`
- Remove `.only` once tests pass

## Conventions
- Use `{ timeout: 20000 }` for assertions that wait on backend responses
- Use `{ force: true }` when selecting files via hidden inputs
- Drag-and-drop: `cy.get('div.cloning-history').selectFile(path, { action: 'drag-drop' })`
- Check warnings/errors in `#global-error-message-wrapper`
- No mocking of backend requests in integration tests — assert on UI state
